    "body": "## Motivation\n\nA local Muse Spark `generation_config.json` with `do_sample: true` and `top_k: 0` produces HTTP 400 in the Python serving path. Interpret the Transformers zero sentinel as disabled top-k filtering for Muse Spark.\n\n## Modifications\n\nKeep the policy in `model_overrides/muse_spark.py`. Resolve its providers once when the tokenizer manager initializes, then apply the alias after sampling parameters are merged and before `SamplingParams` is constructed. Positive top-k values, request precedence, greedy sampling and other models retain their behavior. No test files are added or modified in the final diff.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- **Real-checkpoint GSM8K smoke on 4 GB300 GPUs:** the unmodified base returned the exact top-k-zero HTTP 400. With the patch, all **16/16 requests returned HTTP 200**, with no retries or truncations and real speculative counters on every response. The numeric answer check matched **15/16** references; this is a bounded serving sanity check, not a full accuracy evaluation.\n- Both live phases used identical commands, weights, runtime, prompts and a separate model view with literal `top_k: 0`, `do_sample: true`, temperature 1 and top-p 1. Requests omitted all four sampling fields. DFLASH8, block verification, xhigh reasoning and `--sampling-defaults model` were enabled; no simulated acceptance. The original checkpoint config still has top-k 64 and was not modified.\n- **34 private regression probes passed**; the same probe reproduces eight Muse-zero validation failures on the pristine base. Relevant existing CPU tests: **409 passed plus 331 subtests**, one skipped. One pre-existing whitelist assertion about `mm_enable_dp_encoder` fails identically on the base and is left untouched.\n- Scoped pinned isort, Ruff check/format and codespell checks passed. Source/model identity checks and owned-process cleanup passed; no OOM events or resource-limit violations.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run; no throughput or latency claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format the changed code.\n- [ ] Add unit tests if required.\n- [ ] Update documentation if required.\n- [x] Provide live accuracy validation if required.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38798142926](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38798142926)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38798142812](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38798142812)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38798142847](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38798142847)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
